                <pb facs="1097" n="987" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg987"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.5034 Business Tax/2: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-02-20T17:00:00-05:00">February 20, 1931—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>62. Your 71, February 16, 7 p.m. Department approves your February 16, 6 p.m. to
                    Hankow.</p>
                <p>Authorize Hankow to inform the Chairman of the Hupeh Provincial Government that
                    the regulations cannot be considered applicable to American firms.</p>
                <p>Report developments fully by mail.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
